The engine says which panel a skill belongs in
==============================================

The page can group skills into libraries, but it can only group by what the engine tells it, and the
engine was saying nothing: `list_local_skills` returned a name, a description and a tier. So the last
commit's three panels could not work — every skill fell through the catch-all into the first one.

The manifest's `owner` value is the only place that can say who made a skill, so it is now read and
passed through, and a skill found by walking the bundled directory without a manifest entry is
`quixidesk` — what upstream shipped — while the Hermes roots are `hermes`.

Nothing about discovery changed. This is one field on a JSON object that was already being built.

